<DocsLayout title="Reachability" kicker="02 / getting started" description="Construct shortcuts for exact reachability queries, then verify the preservation invariant explicitly.">
  <h2>Canonical workflow</h2>
  <pre><code>from reachq.generators import random_dag
from reachq.invariants import assert_reachability_preserved
from reachq.reachability import bfs_reachability, parallel_bfs
from reachq.shortcut import build_shortcut_set_for_reachability

graph = random_dag(n=100, edge_probability=0.1, random_seed=42)
shortcuts, beta, realised_bound = build_shortcut_set_for_reachability(
    graph, omega=3.0, random_seed=42,
)
assert_reachability_preserved(graph, shortcuts)
source = graph.vertices()[0]
assert parallel_bfs(graph, source, shortcuts) == bfs_reachability(graph, source)</code></pre>
  <h2>What the return values mean</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>shortcuts</code> is a set of directed vertex pairs.</li>
    <li><code>beta</code> is the asymptotic target quantity used by the construction.</li>
    <li><code>realised_bound</code> is the bound derived by the executed recursion and is the value tests should use.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><code>parallel_bfs</code> currently simulates the reachability primitive sequentially. Construction-level process dispatch is opt-in and should be benchmarked for the graph size at hand.</p>
</DocsLayout>
